A||N||5||LemonSky||What's that squeaking sound?||||5||
Z||000000||LemonSky||11-18-2000||12:27 AM||||Hi, everyone, I own a 1986 SE6, and I've noticed that a squeaking noise emanates from the engine when, 1) the car initially starts in wet weather 2) the A/C turns on when the engine is cool, and 3) the car initially starts in cold weather.<BR>Obviously, it's a belt, but due to my rudimentary knowledge of auto repair, I don't know which one. Thanks in advance for any info.||||reg||5
Z||000001||2xsess||11-18-2000||12:44 AM||||There is only two belts on the V6, So usually it would be best to go ahead and change both of them.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||11-18-2000||02:43 AM||||Its your alt belt....Im plagued w/the same prob right now. Very common Fiero problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||11-18-2000||02:44 AM||||oops, double post...everytime I use my laptop I get this problem..oh well.<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 11-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-18-2000||12:36 PM||||simple replace both belts. if one is going the other isn't far behind. you have to take both off to get to the one anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||11-18-2000||02:22 PM||||I beg to differ.  But I can't, when these guys are right!  Chalk up another vote (mine)for replacing both belts at the same time.<P>Plan on removing the RR wheel+tire, the RR inner fender, and replacing both belts with good quality replacement belts.  To make it easier, use the J.C. Witless / Harbor Fright belt tightening tool.  It's really no big deal, but if it's your first time, it could be an all-day job.  Point is, it's enough trouble, that you <B>will</B> want to replace <B>both</B> belts.  Good time to paint the timing mark and do some general cleanup, too.   <P>Do a search in the archives, using "belt" in the subject line, and you'll gain a lot of useful knowledge. ||||reg||1
